BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New York Women in Film & Television (NYWIFT) - Breaking the Frame 
 - How Far Have Women in Film Really Come? 🎟️
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261017T160000
DTSTAMP:20260914T020231Z
UID:6aa1be5d4a562fb0e741ea94@woodstockfilmfestival.org
DESCRIPTION:As the film industry continues to evolve\, so too have the opp
 ortunities for women behind and in front of the camera. From the pioneers 
 who opened doors to today’s filmmakers redefining storytelling\, this co
 nversation celebrates how far the industry has come\, the progress being m
 ade\, and the opportunities that lie ahead. Through personal experiences a
 nd industry insights\, leading filmmakers will explore the changing landsc
 ape for women in film\, the conversations that can help move the industry 
 forward\, and how the next generation can continue breaking the frame and 
 creating new possibilities for women in the industry.\n\nAre you available
  to participate? If so\, please let myself\, as well as Rashiek Smart and 
 Catherine from NYWIFT and Meira Blaustein from the Woodstock Film Festival
  (all cc here) know at your earliest and send your short bio (50 words or 
 less) and hi res photo to be included in the festival guide. I will be sen
 ding within a month a series of questions we will explore and we have the 
 capacity to feature clips of your work as well. So please prepare to send 
 us a two-minute clip to showcase.\n\n🎟️ Tickets Available\n\n🔗 htt
 ps://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1be5d4a562fb0e74
 1ea94
LOCATION:Utopia Studios
URL:https://woodstockfilmfestival.org/2026-all-events?eventId=6aa1be5d4a56
 2fb0e741ea94
END:VEVENT
